    "model_design": "Add self.short_conv = nn.Conv1d(hidden_units, hidden_units, kernel_size=5, dilation=1, padding=0), giving a 64-to-64 shallow causal residual branch at the current width; construct it after existing initialization inside torch.random.fork_rng(devices=[]) and zero its weights and bias so branch creation preserves the parent's random state and initial computation. In encode_sequence, retain input_x = x immediately after the existing dropout and masking, execute the unchanged block loop, compute local = self.short_conv(nn.functional.pad(input_x.transpose(1, 2), (4, 0))).transpose(1, 2), then fuse with x = (x + local) * mask before returning self.norm(x) * mask, providing a direct trainable path from the current and four preceding embeddings without future leakage. Preserve the current position-free item embeddings and initialization, eight independent gated residual blocks, dilations [1,2,4,8,1,2,4,8], local/dilated fusion, learned residual scales initialized to 0.1, normalization, activations, dropout placement, masking, last-nonpadding selection, and tied scoring; historical findings motivate zero initialization without adding depth aggregation, weight sharing, positional changes, or another gate. Keep MAXLEN=128, HIDDEN_UNITS=64, NUM_BLOCKS=8, KERNEL_SIZE=3, DROPOUT_RATE=0.2, LR=0.001, WEIGHT_DECAY=0.00001, BATCH_SIZE=128, training seed 2024, validation negative-sampling seed 42, identical splits and candidates, and all host preprocessing, BPR loss, Adam, clipping, epochs, checkpoint selection, training, evaluation, and checkpoint/score generation unchanged. Preserve all existing variable names and constructor, forward, encode_sequence, and score_candidates signatures and output shapes, retain exactly the three permitted imports, eight numeric constants, and two classes with methods only, add no model-side I/O, printing, training, evaluation, or CSV generation, and allocate one of the 44 candidate slots for the host to compare validation HR@10 against 0.665, treating 0.675 as an unverified two-additional-hit target on 200 users without test-metric access.",
